(6000183, 876454, 35357, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by David Ey:</b></div><hr/><i> I didn''t realize a collaboration was allowable in one of these open contests.  It''d be interesting to know how many of these   collaborators voted on this fine entry....if sc would care to check. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The DPL system doesn''t allow people on the same team to vote on one anothers'' entries, while the private team thread is there for creative collaboration.  It''s fun, you should try it.  DPL teamwork and feedback is a great thing, though I do also believe the DPL may raise the bar unfairly compared to those who are not on a team.  I think this has been discussed somewhere before.</td>', 'Originally posted by David Ey: I didn''t realize a collaboration was allowable in one of these open contests.  It''d be interesting to know how many of these   collaborators voted on this fine entry....if sc would care to check.  The DPL system doesn''t allow people on the same team to vote on one anothers'' entries, while the private team thread is there for creative collaboration.  It''s fun, you should try it.  DPL teamwork and feedback is a great thing, though I do also believe the DPL may raise the bar unfairly compared to those who are not on a team.  I think this has been discussed somewhere before.', '2010-05-10 14:52:17.000000', NULL, 0),
